// A grand staff where BOTH staves rest the same bars: the run collapses, and EVERY
// staff prints its own multi-measure rest with its own count above it.
//
// In LilyPond the multi-measure-rest engraver lives in the Staff context, so a run
// (which only forms when every staff rests) yields one Multi_measure_rest per staff.
// Verified on 2.24.4 with a PianoStaff resting R1*4 in both staves: two church rests,
// two "4"s, and the interior bar lines gone on both staves.
//
// Lily# emitted only ONE symbol — placed on the top staff — while suppressing the
// per-bar rest glyphs across ALL staves, so every staff below the first came out blank.
// This is the pair to test/multi-measure-rest-grandstaff, which locks in the OPPOSITE
// case: when only one staff rests, nothing merges and the bar lines stay.
//
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/multi-measure-rest-engraver.cc (Staff context), lily/multi-measure-rest.cc.
title "Multi-Measure Rest (grand staff, both staves rest)"
composer "Lily#"

time 4/4
key c major

part melody
part lh { clef bass }

section Main {
  melody {
    c4 d e f |
    R1*4 |
    g4 a b c |
  }
  lh {
    c2 c |
    R1*4 |
    c2 c |
  }
}

form main { Main }

score main "mmr-grandstaff-both-rest" {
  staff melody
  staff lh
}
